          "title": "Ashley",
          "text": "<div>Working as a curator in an art museum, l'm often asked if l'm also an artist. My response has been, \"No, not really.\" But after a conversation with a friend, I realized that's not entirely true. Curating exhibitions, arranging works of art to tell a story, and making design decisions are all creative acts and forms of art.</div><div><br></div><div>I see a similar process reflected in my dissertation writing, particularly in the literature review. A literature review involves analyzing and synthesizing existing research, identifying gaps in the field, and positioning one's own contribution. When drafting mine, I could not decide on the best order to present some of the sections. To work through this, I printed out my writing, cut it into pieces, and physically rearranged and weaved the sections together (much like arranging works of art in an exhibition) to discover what order told the clearest story.</div>"
