          "text": "<div>My dissertation research focuses on emerging adult play in art museums. Roleplaying, or acting out the role of a person, character, or scenario, is one way museums can encourage play. In this activity, try roleplaying as a curator. Your goal is to select and arrange works of art to tell a story. The collaged works of art you'll work with combine photographs I took on campus during my first year in the PhD program with articles from my literature review.</div><div><br></div><div>Define your exhibition goal. Do you want to display works related by subject matter, color, mood?</div><div><br></div><div>Arrange your exhibition. Select your works of art and add them to the wall. Consider your arrangement. Do you stack the works of art? Place them side by side?</div><div><br></div><div>Write a Curator's Statement. On a post-it note, share what story you want your exhibition to tell.</div><div><br></div><div>Share Your Exhibition. Add your curator's statement on the wall and explore what other visitors shared.</div>"
